  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] (f : E → ℝ),\n  Differentiable ℝ f →\n    ∀ (eta beta B ell : ℝ),\n      0 < eta →\n        ∀ (hbeta : 0 < beta),\n          0 < B →\n            2 ≤ ell →\n              0 < ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) →\n                LipschitzWith ⟨beta, LT.lt.le hbeta⟩ (gradient f) →\n                  ∀ (h xp : E) (r : ℝ),\n                    ‖h - xp‖ ≤ √(↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * eta) →\n                      64 * beta ^ 2 * (ell * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) / B + ell ^ 2) ≤ 1 / eta ^ 2 →\n                        have mu :=\n                          (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => h + √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)).prod\n                            (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E));\n                        have W := fun p =>\n                          Inner.inner ℝ\n                            ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                              (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * r) • (p.1 - h) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * r) • p.2))\n                            (gradient f xp -\n                              gradient f\n                                (h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * r) • (p.1 - h) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * r) • p.2));\n                        have F := fun p => Real.exp (2 * ell * Max.max (|W p| - B) 0) - 1;\n                        Measurable W ∧\n                          Measurable F ∧\n                            MeasureTheory.Integrable F mu ∧\n                              ∫ (p : E × E), F p ∂mu ≤\n                                2 *\n                                  Real.exp\n                                    (-Min.min (B ^ 2 / (40 * beta ^ 2 * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * eta ^ 2))\n                                        (B / (8 * beta * eta)))",
    "statement_sha256": "c5357edb19582fcb44c247f5b7b084e967a9013f2cd32e68ed401e7ec5dd0ce0",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "stdGaussian E is the centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability measure on the finite-dimensional real inner-product space E. Measure.map is actual pushforward and Measure.prod is independent product.",
      "gradient f is the real inner-product gradient operator; Differentiable means differentiability at every point. LipschitzWith beta bounds the output distance by beta times the input distance.",
      "Module.finrank is the finite real dimension. Real.sqrt is the nonnegative square root. Max.max and Min.min are ordinary maximum and minimum of real numbers. Integrable is Bochner integrability; all displayed integrals and exponentials are real-valued.",
      "All local path definitions have been expanded from the compiled theorem type and Lean checked definitional equality."
    ]
  },
